kosha transducer

  -- a finite state transducer: reads input, maintains state, emits output.
  -- emit-triples IS a transducer:
  --   input:  (word, info) stream from the sentence
  --   state:  [current-grade, entity-registry, binding-ledger, grammar-trail]
  --   output: triples [subject, edge, object]
  -- the state encodes the epistemic position: what has been seen, what is active.
  -- each word advances the state and may emit zero or more triples.

  "computation-varga-vishesa"
  "morphism-abheda function-sthita"
  "op-reduce-abheda"
  "fold-yukta map-yukta"
  "recursion-sthita sequence-sthita"
  "domain-computation-sthita"

done
